<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link><description>India News Today: Get latest India news and breaking news from India on Times of India. TOI brings the top news headlines from India on Politics, Elections, Current Affairs and more</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-11-24T11:58:21+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/-2128936835.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:58:21 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[6 years after split, BJP and SAD set to reunite in poll-bound Punjab]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/6-years-after-split-bjp-and-sad-set-to-reunite-in-poll-bound-punjab/articleshow/136121300.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136121300.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The BJP and Shiromani Akali Dal are expected to announce their alliance for the upcoming Punjab assembly elections on Tuesday, with Amit Shah, Nitin Nabin and Sukhbir Singh Badal attending a joint press conference. The parties are expected to unveil their seat-sharing formula, with the BJP likely to contest more than the 23 seats it contested under their previous alliance.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/6-years-after-split-bjp-and-sad-set-to-reunite-in-poll-bound-punjab/articleshow/136121300.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/6-years-after-split-bjp-and-sad-set-to-reunite-in-poll-bound-punjab/articleshow/136121300.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T11:37:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136121529,imgsize-932037.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Intention behind withdrawing papa’s security': Gandhis revisit concerns before Rajiv killing]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/papas-security-was-removed-so-that-he-got-killed-sonia-recalls-rahuls-warning-over-rajiv-gandhis-security/articleshow/136120066.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136120066.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Sonia Gandhi has alleged that former Prime Minister Rajiv Gandhi’s security was deliberately withdrawn to facilitate his assassination. In a conversation with Rahul and Priyanka Gandhi about her book ‘Belonging: A Journey of Love’, she recalled raising concerns over his safety, including during a Bihar tour. Rahul also alleged that there was an intention behind the decision, saying his mother had left out some details from the book.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/papas-security-was-removed-so-that-he-got-killed-sonia-recalls-rahuls-warning-over-rajiv-gandhis-security/articleshow/136120066.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/papas-security-was-removed-so-that-he-got-killed-sonia-recalls-rahuls-warning-over-rajiv-gandhis-security/articleshow/136120066.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T10:41:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136120906,imgsize-1289939.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘No one should be exempted from law’: Congress presses ally Vijay over collector's complaint against TVK MLA]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-one-should-be-exempted-from-law-congress-presses-ally-vijay-over-collectors-complaint-against-tvk-mla/articleshow/136119642.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136119642.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Congress MP Manickam Tagore and DMK MP Kanimozhi have demanded action against TVK MLA C Arun Vignesh after the Kallakurichi district collector filed a police complaint against him over alleged inappropriate behaviour. Kanimozhi questioned Chief Minister Vijay over the delay in acting against his party MLA. Meanwhile, the NCW has sought a fair probe and an action-taken report from the Tamil Nadu DGP within seven days.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-one-should-be-exempted-from-law-congress-presses-ally-vijay-over-collectors-complaint-against-tvk-mla/articleshow/136119642.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-one-should-be-exempted-from-law-congress-presses-ally-vijay-over-collectors-complaint-against-tvk-mla/articleshow/136119642.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T10:12:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136119716,imgsize-501427.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[SP’s ‘Jan-Man Manifesto’: Akhilesh Yadav to unveil 2027 poll roadmap on Constitution Day]]></title><description><![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sps-jan-man-manifesto-akhilesh-yadav-to-unveil-2027-poll-roadmap-on-constitution-day/articleshow/136119297.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sps-jan-man-manifesto-akhilesh-yadav-to-unveil-2027-poll-roadmap-on-constitution-day/articleshow/136119297.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T10:08:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Subhadra Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136119652,imgsize-99888.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Distorted portrayal': Sonia Gandhi gets legal notice over VD Savarkar's remarks in memoir]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/distorted-portrayal-sonia-gandhi-gets-legal-notice-over-vd-savarkars-remarks-in-memoir/articleshow/136117842.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136117842.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Vinayak Damodar Savarkar's grandnephew, Satyaki Savarkar, issued a legal notice to Congress leader Sonia Gandhi about her memoir statements. He demands an unconditional apology and correction regarding her portrayal of Savarkar. The notice contends that the statements are historically inaccurate and prejudicial to Savarkar's legacy. It references historical contexts that allegedly contradict the claims made in her book.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/distorted-portrayal-sonia-gandhi-gets-legal-notice-over-vd-savarkars-remarks-in-memoir/articleshow/136117842.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/distorted-portrayal-sonia-gandhi-gets-legal-notice-over-vd-savarkars-remarks-in-memoir/articleshow/136117842.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T08:31:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Kanchan Yadav</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136118056,imgsize-96730.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[6 samples collected, 5 met applicable standards: Bisleri]